-- title:
--   Order of a finite Hopf algebra map: kernel times image
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, and let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings carrying Hopf $k$-algebra structures, each finite as a $k$-module. Let $\varphi \colon A \to B$ be a $k$-bialgebra homomorphism (a $k$-algebra map that is simultaneously a morphism of coalgebras). Write $\varepsilon_A \colon A \to k$ for the counit, viewed as a $k$-algebra homomorphism, and let $\mathfrak{a} = \varphi(\ker \varepsilon_A)B$ be the ideal of $B$ generated by the image under the underlying algebra map of $\varphi$ of the augmentation ideal $\ker \varepsilon_A$. Then the $k$-dimension of $B$ factors as $$\dim_k B = \dim_k\bigl(B/\mathfrak{a}\bigr)\cdot \dim_k \varphi(A),$$ where $\varphi(A)$ is the range of $\varphi$ as a $k$-subalgebra of $B$ and all dimensions are `Module.finrank` over $k$. No cocommutativity, freeness beyond that automatic over a field, or reducedness hypothesis is imposed, and the characteristic of $k$ is arbitrary.
--
--   In the language of finite group schemes over $k$, with $u \colon \operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ the morphism dual to $\varphi$, this is the counted form of the first isomorphism theorem: $|G| = |\ker u| \cdot |\operatorname{im} u|$, since $\operatorname{Spec}(B/\mathfrak{a})$ is the scheme-theoretic kernel and $\operatorname{Spec} \varphi(A)$ the scheme-theoretic image. It is used in the modular-curve part of the development to compute orders of finite flat group schemes arising from level-torsion and Raynaud quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_finrank_eq_finrank_quotient_map_ker_counit_mul_finrank_range.lean

import Mathlib

